## Design Decision: No Hardcoded Equipment Limits

All thresholds that control equipment are user-configurable via Web UI. The only non-configurable values are physical safety limits (`SAFETY_HUM_CEILING_HARD` at 95%) that act as emergency brakes — they don't control normal operation, they prevent disaster.

---

Here's what needs to change:

---

## 1. `config.h`

**Change `SAFETY_HUM_CEILING_HARD` from 90 to 95:**
```cpp
#define SAFETY_HUM_CEILING_HARD         95.0f   // Emergency cutoff — never exceeded
```
This stays as a non-configurable last-resort safety. It doesn't control equipment — it's an emergency brake if everything else fails.

**Add the new exhaust threshold default:**
```cpp
#define DEFAULT_HUM_EXHAUST_ON          92.0f   // Exhaust fan ON above this (user-configurable)
```

---

## 2. `automation.h`

**Add to `AutomationThresholds` struct:**
```cpp
  float humExhaustOn;  // High humidity exhaust trigger (user-configurable)
```

**Add function declaration:**
```cpp
void automation_runHighHumidityExhaust();
```

---

## 3. `automation.cpp`

**Add to `automation_loadDefaults()`:**
```cpp
    g_thresholds.humExhaustOn = DEFAULT_HUM_EXHAUST_ON;
```

**Add validation in `automation_updateThresholds()`:**
```cpp
    if (newThresholds->humExhaustOn < 0 || newThresholds->humExhaustOn > 100) return;
    if (newThresholds->humExhaustOn <= newThresholds->humCeiling) return;
```

**Add the new function before `automation_runCO2Loop()`:**
```cpp
void automation_runHighHumidityExhaust() {
    if (g_systemState.calibrationActive) return;
    if (automation_isHumidityOverrideActive()) return;

    float currentHumidity = sensors_isHumidityValid() ?
        g_systemState.currentHumidity : g_systemState.lastKnownGoodHumidity;

    if (currentHumidity > g_thresholds.humExhaustOn) {
        if (!relayManager_isRelayOn(RELAY_EXHAUST)) {
            relayManager_setRelay(RELAY_EXHAUST, true);
        }
    } else if (currentHumidity <= g_thresholds.humCeiling) {
        if (relayManager_isRelayOn(RELAY_EXHAUST)) {
            uint16_t currentCO2 = sensors_isCO2Valid() ?
                g_systemState.currentCO2 : g_systemState.lastKnownGoodCO2;
            if (currentCO2 <= g_thresholds.co2LowTarget) {
                relayManager_setRelay(RELAY_EXHAUST, false);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

---

## 4. `web_ui.cpp` — HTML

**Add exhaust threshold input in Config tab (before Ceiling row):**
```html
    <div class="config-row"><label>Exhaust ON (%)</label><input type="number" id="humExhaustOn" value="92" step="1"></div>
```

---

## 5. `web_ui.cpp` — JavaScript

**Add to `updateConfig()`:**
```javascript
  document.getElementById('humExhaustOn').value = msg.humExhaustOn;
```

**Add to `saveThresholds()`:**
```javascript
  var exhaustOn = parseFloat(document.getElementById('humExhaustOn').value);
```
Add `exhaustOn` to the NaN check and the thresholds object.

---

## 6. `web_ui.cpp` — C++ WebSocket handlers

**Add to `sendConfigUpdate()`:**
```cpp
  doc["humExhaustOn"] = t->humExhaustOn;
```

**Add to thresholds command handler:**
```cpp
        newThresholds.humExhaustOn = doc["data"]["humExhaustOn"] | thresholds->humExhaustOn;
```

---

## 7. `.ino` main loop

**Add call after `automation_runCO2Loop()`:**
```cpp
  automation_runHighHumidityExhaust();
```

